{"duration_api_ms":118715,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"7ee30833-d8eb-4409-bb9c-7675f133cb22","total_cost_usd":0.197154,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16830,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":12983,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":7177},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16830,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":12983,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16830,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16830},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":12983,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":16830,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.197154,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":7177,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The front is a one-parameter ridge at D~3.3852, bluntness 1.2, cone 70. The gamma sweep runs from -1.5 (flux 227k, T 417.9) to -3.5703 (flux 274.6k, T 391.1). max_g pins the steep end at gamma about -3.5703, and mass fraction pins D at about 3.3852. Hypervolume has plateaued at 0.3556, and 9 of the last 20 rows show gains of under 1e-4. Bluntness above 1.2 or cone below 70 has repeatedly returned extrapolation or geometry failures. Only the gamma ridge remains safe to sample.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-b8e5f12114a1 to C-c461ce8af13c: flux and T vary smoothly and monotonically with gamma at fixed geometry (flux 227.2k to 274.6k, T 417.87 to 391.08).\",\"C-c461ce8af13c has max_g margin 1.9e-5 and C-8187cef72ab8 (gamma -3.5704) has -1.4e-5, so the g limit sits at gamma about -3.57031.\",\"D=3.385 gives mass margin 1.449e-4 (C-163399613c78) and D=3.3852 gives 9.05e-6, so the mass limit is at D about 3.38521 if the slope of about -0.68 per m is linear.\",\"C-05edbf22eaa2, C-7db223121090, C-3d41ce848a30 and C-3136d3bd2588 failed cd_fore extrapolation with bluntness above 1.2 or cone below 70. C-e0197c1bd7dc and C-5608a135cebc failed on geometry. The buildable, in-hull region is only the corner (1.2, 70).\",\"C-956957ec60d4, C-7112b6b29bcf and C-14444dd6b10a show lower bluntness breaks the mass-fraction limit and raises flux, so they are worse.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak g is set almost entirely by gamma, which fixes the steep end of the ridge. Mass fraction scales with D^2 and rises with lower bluntness or cone, which fixes D at the corner. A larger D and higher Cd lower the ballistic coefficient, so flux and T both fall. Shallower gamma lowers flux but lengthens the heat pulse and raises T. That gives a convex flux-T curve in gamma. I expect no unexplored region to dominate, so I fill the gaps between known gamma points to sharpen the front. I also test D=3.38521, the last feasible step in D, at several gammas.\",\"uncertainty\":\"I am interpolating linearly between neighbouring ridge points, so predictions are good to about 0.05 K and 300 W/m2. The D=3.38521 points could break the mass limit if the mass-margin slope is nonlinear. Near gamma -3.5702 the g margin is about 1e-5 and a small D change could flip it. Some of my gamma values may duplicate unseen evaluated rows, since only part of the 60-point front is shown. I am relying on the shown data plus generic ballistic-entry reasoning. Hypervolume gains will be tiny.\",\"proposals\":[\n{\"parent_id\":\"C-b8e5f12114a1\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the ridge between gamma -1.5 and -1.65.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.5714},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":228620,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":416.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the shallow-end gap of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},\n{\"parent_id\":\"C-b8e5f12114a1\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the ridge between gamma -1.65 and -1.88.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.7423},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":232100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413.96,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the gap between existing front points.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},\n{\"parent_id\":\"C-b8e5f12114a1\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the ridge between gamma -1.88 and -2.1.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.9317},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":236090,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":411.02,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the gap between existing front points.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},\n{\"parent_id\":\"C-b8e5f12114a1\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the ridge between gamma -1.88 and -2.1.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.0261},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":238160,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":409.62,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the gap between existing front points.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},\n{\"parent_id\":\"C-b8e5f12114a1\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the ridge between gamma -2.2 and -2.37.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.2731},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":243730,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":406.08,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the gap between existing front points.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},\n{\"paren